An antibody molecule produced by B-lymphocytes is a Y-shaped molecule:
- it has **four peptide chains**, so it is represented as \(\text{H}_2\text{L}_2\);
- **two small chains**, called **light chains**;
- **two longer chains**, called **heavy chains**;
- the chains are held together by **disulphide bonds** (S-S), between the two heavy chains and between each heavy chain and its light chain;
- each arm carries an **antigen binding site** at the N-terminal (amino) end, formed by the tips of a heavy and a light chain.

The structure can also be shown as a labelled Y-shaped diagram marking the light chains, the heavy chains, the antigen binding sites and the disulphide bonds; the marking scheme gives the same credit for a correctly labelled diagram.

Any four of the measures taken up by NACO (National AIDS Control Organisation), WHO and other NGOs:
- ensuring the use of **HIV-free blood** in blood banks;
- ensuring the use of only **disposable needles and syringes** in public and private hospitals and clinics;
- **free distribution of condoms**;
- **controlling drug abuse**;
- advocating **safe sex**;
- promoting **regular check-ups for HIV** in susceptible populations;
- preventing infection during blood transfusions;
- monitoring of pregnant women for HIV.

Draw an **inverted pyramid of number**, with one bar for each trophic level:
- bottom (narrowest) bar: **1 banyan tree**, the **producer** (first trophic level);
- middle bar: **20 insects** feeding on the tree, the **primary consumers** (herbivores, second trophic level);
- top (widest) bar: **32 birds** feeding on the insects, the **secondary consumers** (third trophic level).

Description: a pyramid of number shows the number of individuals at each trophic level. Here a single large tree supports many insects, which in turn support even more birds, so the number increases towards the top and the pyramid is **inverted**. The marking scheme gives 1 mark for the correct trophic levels and 1 mark for the correct inverted diagram.

Parturition is induced by a complex **neuroendocrine mechanism**:
- the signals for parturition originate from the **fully developed foetus and the placenta**;
- these induce mild uterine contractions called the **foetal ejection reflex**;
- this triggers the release of **oxytocin** from the maternal pituitary;
- oxytocin acts on the uterine muscle and causes **stronger uterine contractions**;
- these in turn stimulate **further secretion of oxytocin**;
- the stimulatory reflex between the uterine contraction and oxytocin secretion continues, resulting in **stronger and stronger contractions**, which lead to the expulsion of the baby out of the uterus through the birth canal.

Any three advantages of genetically modified plants:
- crops are made **more tolerant to abiotic stresses** (cold, drought, salt, heat);
- **reduced reliance on chemical pesticides** (pest-resistant crops, such as Bt cotton);
- they help to **reduce post-harvest losses**;
- **increased efficiency of mineral usage** by plants, which prevents early exhaustion of fertility of the soil;
- **enhanced nutritional value of food**, for example golden rice, a vitamin 'A' enriched rice;
- tailor-made plants supply alternative resources to industries, in the form of starches, fuels and pharmaceuticals.

(i) When resources in the habitat are **unlimited**, each species has the ability to realise fully its innate potential to grow in number. The population then grows in an **exponential or geometric fashion**: the larger the population becomes, the faster it grows. Plotting population density against time gives a **J-shaped curve**.

(ii) If, in a population of size N, the birth rate (per capita births) is b and the death rate (per capita deaths) is d, then the change in N during a unit time period t is \(\frac{dN}{dt} = (b - d) \times N\). Let \(b - d = r\); then \(\frac{dN}{dt} = rN\), which integrates to \(N_t = N_0 e^{rt}\), where
- N = size of the population (\(N_t\) at time t, \(N_0\) at time zero);
- r = the **intrinsic rate of natural increase**, an important parameter for assessing the impact of any biotic or abiotic factor on population growth;
- b = birth rate and d = death rate;
- e = the base of natural logarithms (2.71828).

(iii) The curve is the **exponential growth curve** (J-shaped curve). The graph has population size (N) on the y-axis and time (t) on the x-axis; the curve starts low, rises slowly at first and then more and more steeply, giving the shape of a J.
